  │      Module      │                          Responsibility                           │
  ├──────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mstore.js[39m         │ Owns state. Every mutation is a named method that emits an event. │
  ├──────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mevents.js[39m        │ ~20-line pub/sub. No dependencies.                                │
  ├──────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153msubscribers.js[39m   │ Pure function: [38;5;153m(task, event) → userIds to notify[39m.                 │
  ├──────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mnotifications.js[39m │ Listens to events, creates records, marks read.                   │
  ├──────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mpersist.js[39m       │ localStorage load/save.                                           │
  ├──────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mui/*.js[39m          │ [38;5;153mtask-list[39m, [38;5;153mbell[39m, [38;5;153mtoast[39m, [38;5;153muser-switcher[39m. Render only.               │
  └──────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  [1mData model:[0m

  [34mUser[39m         { id, name }
  [34mTask[39m         { id, title, status, assigneeId, creatorId, watcherIds[] }
  [34mChangeEvent[39m  { id, type, taskId, actorId, at, field, [34mfrom[39m, to }
  [34mNotification[39m { id, userId, eventId, read }

  [1mOne deliberate choice worth flagging: a [38;5;153mNotification[39m stores an [38;5;153meventId[39m, not a rendered message string.[0m The tempting
  shortcut is to store [38;5;153m"Alice reassigned Fix login to you"[39m at creation time. Don't — then wording changes require
  migrating stored records, and the notification can't re-render from the current user's perspective. Storing the event
  and rendering at display time keeps text a pure view concern. It costs one indirection and buys a lot.

  [38;5;153msubscribers.js[39m being a [1mpure function[0m is the other one — it's the actual logic of the feature (roles ∪ watchers, minus
  the actor), and keeping it free of DOM and storage means it's trivially testable without a browser.

  ---

  Does this structure look right before I move on to the notification rules and UI behavior?

